(1611852, 217113, 39850, '<td valign="top">''8'' (only pretend and fyi) - Wow - but is this rain? Challengewise if I were voting, I would ''pass'' it as rain even just for the ''illusion'' or ''emulation'' (IF not rain) - it is almost like a macro of a ''heavy'' rain ''drop''.  I have never seen a water droplet (or whatever the correct term is) shot like this.  The coloring, and indeed effect within the ''drop'' (including the ''stem'') is incredible.  The ''sparkle'' on the edge too... wow, but my cynicism just will not let me believe this is an actual raindrop captured naturally outdoors....if you have, I will be speechless.  Great shot, but Challengewise, well, will wait and see what it is when the Challenge is over.  Amazing shot at any rate, very nice.  Criticism; wish it were at least 640 in height, and possibly in width.  Perhaps that top right ''parted'' droplet out of frame, maybe might have made this even better, not sure.  Adding to favorites for inspiration. edit:typos<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-08-22 06:32:10.</i></td>', '''8'' (only pretend and fyi) - Wow - but is this rain? Challengewise if I were voting, I would ''pass'' it as rain even just for the ''illusion'' or ''emulation'' (IF not rain) - it is almost like a macro of a ''heavy'' rain ''drop''.  I have never seen a water droplet (or whatever the correct term is) shot like this.  The coloring, and indeed effect within the ''drop'' (including the ''stem'') is incredible.  The ''sparkle'' on the edge too... wow, but my cynicism just will not let me believe this is an actual raindrop captured naturally outdoors....if you have, I will be speechless.  Great shot, but Challengewise, well, will wait and see what it is when the Challenge is over.  Amazing shot at any rate, very nice.  Criticism; wish it were at least 640 in height, and possibly in width.  Perhaps that top right ''parted'' droplet out of frame, maybe might have made this even better, not sure.  Adding to favorites for inspiration. edit:typos', '2005-08-15 09:55:52.000000', '2005-08-22 07:32:10.000000', 1),
(1611857, 217779, 39850, '<td valign="top">''6'' - Nice shot for the Challenge.  The b/w works well.  Criticism; I would like to see more ''blur'' but you''d likely lose the rain more.  Something to bring out the rain drops more than the fence and ''passer by'' (somehow, no idea how) would make this shot have more impact (specially for the Challenge) in my opinion.  Maybe an ''unusual'' cropping somehow, not sure.</td>', '''6'' - Nice shot for the Challenge.  The b/w works well.  Criticism; I would like to see more ''blur'' but you''d likely lose the rain more.  Something to bring out the rain drops more than the fence and ''passer by'' (somehow, no idea how) would make this shot have more impact (specially for the Challenge) in my opinion.  Maybe an ''unusual'' cropping somehow, not sure.', '2005-08-15 09:58:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(1611865, 217932, 39850, '<td valign="top">''6'' - Fairly good capture of the rain for the Challenge.  Criticism; for me, a totally different crop and focus here would have made this a real abstract type of shot.  Perhaps, losing the car altogether, gaining a slightly different angle to get the curve of the path, and the gutter at the top of frame.  I just see potential here for a kind of ''abstract'' type of shot using the two contrasting colors and the seemingly ''pouring rain''.  Just my ''viewpoint'' and ''opinion''.  edit:typos &amp; clarification<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-08-22 06:43:35.</i></td>', '''6'' - Fairly good capture of the rain for the Challenge.  Criticism; for me, a totally different crop and focus here would have made this a real abstract type of shot.  Perhaps, losing the car altogether, gaining a slightly different angle to get the curve of the path, and the gutter at the top of frame.  I just see potential here for a kind of ''abstract'' type of shot using the two contrasting colors and the seemingly ''pouring rain''.  Just my ''viewpoint'' and ''opinion''.  edit:typos & clarification', '2005-08-15 10:01:58.000000', '2005-08-22 07:43:35.000000', 1),
(1611868, 217880, 31403, '<td valign="top">this is a great take on the challenge.  I would think the focus should be on her, since people are very interesting and a blurred garden still communicates "garden", love her darkness vs the light outside, migh turn her head a little so we can see more of her face - just a thought, nice image</td>', 'this is a great take on the challenge.  I would think the focus should be on her, since people are very interesting and a blurred garden still communicates "garden", love her darkness vs the light outside, migh turn her head a little so we can see more of her face - just a thought, nice image', '2005-08-15 10:03:49.000000', NULL, 1),
