(1627778, 215592, 17837, '<td valign="top">The exposure and lighting just arent doing it.I see you fired a flash, but perhaps you needed to light the inside of the room as well to get a good exposure.</td>', 'The exposure and lighting just arent doing it.I see you fired a flash, but perhaps you needed to light the inside of the room as well to get a good exposure.', '2005-08-21 10:43:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(1627783, 217211, 17837, '<td valign="top">I think this photo would fair extremely well as a macro shot, or closer up. Also, learn to set the white balance! It''s an easy tool, and very valuable. The photo has a blue tint to it, caused from the flash.</td>', 'I think this photo would fair extremely well as a macro shot, or closer up. Also, learn to set the white balance! It''s an easy tool, and very valuable. The photo has a blue tint to it, caused from the flash.', '2005-08-21 10:47:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(1627787, 217808, 40295, '<td valign="top">I like the effect - and catching the raindrops on the tips of the tassels works very well - I do think a bit more of a crop taking away more ofhte bottom of the image would have helped accentuate the rain effect.</td>', 'I like the effect - and catching the raindrops on the tips of the tassels works very well - I do think a bit more of a crop taking away more ofhte bottom of the image would have helped accentuate the rain effect.', '2005-08-21 10:50:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(1627788, 217155, 17837, '<td valign="top">another cool lightning shot, though over exposed. Perhaps a larger aperture (usually around f/11) works extremely well for lightning, while not blowing out the main bolt. Also, the horizon is tilted.</td>', 'another cool lightning shot, though over exposed. Perhaps a larger aperture (usually around f/11) works extremely well for lightning, while not blowing out the main bolt. Also, the horizon is tilted.', '2005-08-21 10:51:03.000000', NULL, 1),
