(1629496, 216793, 19936, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the comments.  It is always interesting about the b/w vs. color issue as you can see by the comments.  For those interested I converted to b/w so that the flower would not be as prominent.  I wanted the rain to be evident since that was the subject and thought the brightness of the flower was distracting.  And yes, this is a fake.  I rant he sprinkler which created the slanted rain.  Wind would have made it more difficult to get a sharp image.</td>', 'Thanks for all the comments.  It is always interesting about the b/w vs. color issue as you can see by the comments.  For those interested I converted to b/w so that the flower would not be as prominent.  I wanted the rain to be evident since that was the subject and thought the brightness of the flower was distracting.  And yes, this is a fake.  I rant he sprinkler which created the slanted rain.  Wind would have made it more difficult to get a sharp image.', '2005-08-22 01:12:12.000000', NULL, 0),
