(1646770, 217533, 12573, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by maiblossoms:</b></div><hr/><i> Wow, I really love this! This is one of my favorites in this challenge. Because it is abstractish, it seems to convey the mood and feeling of rain really well, rather than just the details of what rain looks like. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Thanks!  This confirms my own feelings about the image.  I had several other outtakes which were more focused, but this to me spoke more about the feeling of a summer storm and the beauty of a well-lit rainy day.</td>', 'Originally posted by maiblossoms: Wow, I really love this! This is one of my favorites in this challenge. Because it is abstractish, it seems to convey the mood and feeling of rain really well, rather than just the details of what rain looks like.  Thanks!  This confirms my own feelings about the image.  I had several other outtakes which were more focused, but this to me spoke more about the feeling of a summer storm and the beauty of a well-lit rainy day.', '2005-08-26 01:45:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(1646806, 216389, 34247, '<td valign="top">outstanding idea and execution.</td>', 'outstanding idea and execution.', '2005-08-26 02:10:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(1646822, 217902, 25355, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by rikki11:</b></div><hr/><i> Too much foreground and not enough subject. Move in closer (or were you sheltering yourself as well?). </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>The title of the challenge being "Rain", the great expanse of foreground is there because it shows the splashy heaviness of the rainshower. This is already a crop of the larger picture.</td>', 'Originally posted by rikki11: Too much foreground and not enough subject. Move in closer (or were you sheltering yourself as well?).   The title of the challenge being "Rain", the great expanse of foreground is there because it shows the splashy heaviness of the rainshower. This is already a crop of the larger picture.', '2005-08-26 02:29:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(1646827, 217902, 25355, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by aguapreta:</b></div><hr/><i> Nice candid, it would have helped if the subjects had been actually doing an activity or focused on something a bit more specific. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Their activity is Waiting for the Rain to Stop; this type of storm is over in quite a short time.</td>', 'Originally posted by aguapreta: Nice candid, it would have helped if the subjects had been actually doing an activity or focused on something a bit more specific.   Their activity is Waiting for the Rain to Stop; this type of storm is over in quite a short time.', '2005-08-26 02:32:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(1647021, 217894, 18552, '<td valign="top">What a cool picture, Judy! It has such atmosphere. I really thought it was taken in a heavy storm in Mexico! Won''t be long now and you''ll be getting a ribbon with great pictures like this.</td>', 'What a cool picture, Judy! It has such atmosphere. I really thought it was taken in a heavy storm in Mexico! Won''t be long now and you''ll be getting a ribbon with great pictures like this.', '2005-08-26 07:59:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(1647034, 216910, 29462, '<td valign="top">It''s interesting really because I really worked at focusing on the pattern of light created by the rain (yes the real thing) I was trying to recreate that sort moment when your not really looking at the scenery or the rain just absorbing the fact it''s raining again.<br/>I obviously missed a great lump that makes a picture appealing to others but given that I''m pleased with the constructive comments from people that took the time to look at the picture, but i am really disappointed by a couple of comments that are not constructive and quit frankly a little insulting I hope that made them feel big</td>', 'It''s interesting really because I really worked at focusing on the pattern of light created by the rain (yes the real thing) I was trying to recreate that sort moment when your not really looking at the scenery or the rain just absorbing the fact it''s raining again.I obviously missed a great lump that makes a picture appealing to others but given that I''m pleased with the constructive comments from people that took the time to look at the picture, but i am really disappointed by a couple of comments that are not constructive and quit frankly a little insulting I hope that made them feel big', '2005-08-26 08:18:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(1647457, 217534, 5112, '<td valign="top">Congratulations, David, it''s good to see you on the front page again!<br/> <br/>My family and I just came back on Tuesday from almost your neck of the woods - we went to WYoming (again!) for about 10 days.  Sure saw a number of scenes like this one.  It''s so beautiful.<br/> <br/>Congratulations again!</td>', 'Congratulations, David, it''s good to see you on the front page again! My family and I just came back on Tuesday from almost your neck of the woods - we went to WYoming (again!) for about 10 days.  Sure saw a number of scenes like this one.  It''s so beautiful. Congratulations again!', '2005-08-26 12:46:02.000000', NULL, 0),
